\title[The ECM self-destruction wall is an accounting artifact]{The ECM Self-Destruction Wall Is an Accounting Artifact\\
\normalsize Exact outcome counts for stage-1 elliptic curve factorization, and a faithfulness criterion for outcome ledgers}

\author{Aristotle}
\date{28 August 2026}

\begin{document}

\begin{abstract}
A recorded claim about the elliptic curve method of factorization (ECM) asserts a \emph{self-destruction wall}: that when the stage-1 smoothness bound satisfies $B_1 \gtrsim \min(p,q)$ for $N=pq$, every Hasse-window group order divides $\lcm(1,\dots,B_1)$, all curves degenerate simultaneously, and the uncapped expected number of curves $\E[T]$ becomes infinite, with an alleged validity edge $B_1 \lesssim \min(p,q)/2$. We prove that the mechanism is correct and its conclusion inverted. Once $B_1 \ge p+1+2\sqrt p$, every Hasse-window order is at most $B_1$, hence $B_1$-powersmooth, hence divides $\lcm(1,\dots,B_1)$; every point of every curve is annihilated modulo $p$, and provided some prime factor of the mod-$q$ order exceeds $B_1$, the guarded inversion returns $\gcd = p$ on \emph{every} trial: success rate $1$, $\E[T]=1$. We show $\E[T] = m/\gcd(m,k(B)) \le m$ at every bound and antitone in $B$, so no infinite-$\E[T]$ regime exists. We locate the genuine destruction regime at $\max(p,q)$, give exact cardinalities for all four separated outcome blocks in the two-prime cyclic model together with an exact reveal count, and exhibit an explicit two-line witness of the real wall. Modelling an accounting scheme as a \emph{ledger} from firing patterns to recorded outcomes, we prove that the outcome-separated ledger is injective while the single conflation ``file any mod-$p$ degeneracy as a death'' is not, and that on precisely the firing pattern generated at the wall it records $\dead$ where the truth is $\found\,p$. A 600-trial sweep at bit length $26$ observed zero deaths and success $1.000$ in every cell at and above the alleged cliff.
\end{abstract}

